    "Parallel small-row FP64 matmul avoids padded GEMM for decode; four-row quantized prefill kernels reuse block decoding and handle partial rows.",
    "Fused HC4 Sinkhorn removes thousands of launches while preserving original float32 rounding boundaries and ordered float64 sums/divisions. Serial decode and parallel prefill variants expose pre/post/comb as borrowed views of one buffer.",
    "Model-scoped immutable Vulkan handles share the original context, allocator and queue. Routed CPU expert SiLU inherits the model contract at load time; no process-wide environment mutation or thread-local policy is used."
  ],
